WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.709
Before your first ride, one question: what should other riders call you?

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.041
A new account is asked straight after its code. Continue waits for a name, then you

00:00:15.041 --> 00:00:17.273
go on to the screen you asked for.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.841
Two to twenty-four letters, digits, spaces, dots, dashes or underscores. Anything

00:00:25.841 --> 00:00:29.412
else is refused, and the field says what's allowed.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.958
The backend holds the one rule. It trims the name and keeps it, or refuses it and

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:38.105
leaves the old name as it was.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:45.936
Profile's headline uses your name, at level one until XP arrives.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.503
Change it from Settings: a dialog opens with your name, and Save updates the

00:00:56.503 --> 00:00:59.567
headline. Cancel or Escape changes nothing.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.590
Phone to desktop, one calm question, and the dialog becomes a sheet.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.985
What the tests prove: no one rides without a name, a bad one is never kept, and a

00:01:16.985 --> 00:01:18.567
new one shows at once.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
